From: knulli <knulli@knulli>
Subject: [PATCH] use an alpha-less texture format for the amiga screen

The emulator draws into amiga_surface without ever setting the alpha
byte, so every pixel it hands to SDL has alpha 0.  Declaring the texture
RGBA32 makes SDL's GLES2 renderer pick the ABGR shader, which writes
that alpha straight through to the framebuffer.  The display engine
composites fb0 per-pixel, so an alpha-0 frame is invisible: correct RGB
in /dev/fb0, black panel.

RGBX32 has the identical byte layout minus the alpha channel, so the
upload is unchanged, but it selects the BGR shader instead, which forces
gl_FragColor.a = 1.0.

SDL_RENDER_DRIVER=software hid this: mali-fbdev has no
CreateWindowFramebuffer, so SDL falls back to SDL_CreateWindowTexture,
which deliberately picks an alpha-less format for the window surface and
therefore already took the a=1.0 path.

--- a/src/osdep/amiberry_gfx.cpp
+++ b/src/osdep/amiberry_gfx.cpp
@@ -384,7 +384,7 @@
 			int width, height;
 			Uint32 format;
 			SDL_QueryTexture(amiga_texture, &format, nullptr, &width, &height);
-			if (width == -w && height == -h && (depth == 16 && format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB565) || (depth == 32 && format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGBA32))
+			if (width == -w && height == -h && (depth == 16 && format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB565) || (depth == 32 && format == SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGBX32))
 			{
 				set_scaling_option(monid, &currprefs, width, height);
 				return true;
@@ -397,7 +397,7 @@
 		SDL_DestroyTexture(amiga_texture);
 
 	AmigaMonitor* mon = &AMonitors[0];
-	amiga_texture = SDL_CreateTexture(mon->amiga_renderer, depth == 16 ? SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB565 : SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGBA32, SDL_TEXTUREACCESS_STREAMING, w, h);
+	amiga_texture = SDL_CreateTexture(mon->amiga_renderer, depth == 16 ? SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB565 : SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGBX32, SDL_TEXTUREACCESS_STREAMING, w, h);
 	return amiga_texture != nullptr;
 #endif
 }
